Wall-mounted plastic soap dispensers are most likely classified in 3924.90 (household articles of plastics) or 3922.90 (other sanitary ware), or in 8479.89 (machines with individual functions), or 9603. CBP rulings on similar manual soap dispensers (e.g., Bobrick, San Jamar) have gone to 3924.90.56 or 3922.90.

San Jamar rulings on soap dispensers: I recall NY rulings classifying plastic manual soap dispensers in 3922.90.0000 ("Other: bathroom fixtures and fittings of plastics"). Wall-mounted plastic soap dispensers for restrooms are bathroom fittings, and 3922 covers "baths, shower-baths, sinks, washbasins, bidets, lavatory pans, seats and covers, flushing cisterns and similar sanitary ware." Soap dishes and toilet-paper holders, towel rails, and similar bathroom fixtures fall under 3922.90 (the Explanatory Notes for 3924 and 3922 mention such fixtures). I'll go with 3922.90.0000.

{"hts_code": "3922.90.0000", "reason": "Wall-mounted plastic manual soap dispensers are restroom fixtures, which fall under plastic sanitary ware and bathroom fittings in heading 3922, other (3922.90)."}
